{"id": "EUVD-2026-86711", "enisaUuid": "775b4013-6bd9-3741-bb50-e760ecd609d6", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nbpf: Mark syscall helpers as sleepable\n\nbpf_sys_bpf() executes the bpf(2) syscall body, which can take mutexes,\nallocate with GFP_KERNEL, and wait for an RCU grace period.\nbpf_sys_close() reaches close_fd() and filp_close(), which can sleep as\nwell.\n\nBoth helpers are limited to BPF_PROG_TYPE_SYSCALL, whose main program is\nsleepable. That does not make every callback sleepable: a syscall program\ncan register a bpf_timer callback, and the verifier checks that callback\nin a non-sleepable context while retaining the syscall helper set.\n\nWithout .might_sleep on the prototypes, such a callback can invoke\nbpf_sys_bpf() from hrtimer softirq context and trigger a\nscheduling-while-atomic failure. bpf_sys_close() is exposed through the\nsame missing context check.\n\nSet .might_sleep on both prototypes so the existing helper-context check\nrejects them from timer callbacks and other atomic regions. Calls from the\nsleepable main body remain valid.", "datePublished": "2026-09-25T10:24:04", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:54:19", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/9496d857205e60241034b798d7745ff8830ba599", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/d8cfe9f71d302970ae393616960f2b3021d2b3b0", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/65f636322ac402add6046c68e9ece77b9ffd71c9", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/3408e98f06ce06ea6a58ca6c39da9c23f0029c06", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/d05524794240b52fdc3b6c1220dd05505715824d"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-98058", "GHSA-24c8-ppg7-5393"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.17, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "020dc4f1-515a-37ef-b43f-bcd84ef5e2a3", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.114"}, {"id": "0a43a1b9-55ea-3d56-861f-0ce2e4612f17", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "79a7f8bdb159d9914b58740f3d31d602a6e4aca8 <65f636322ac402add6046c68e9ece77b9ffd71c9"}, {"id": "2f2aff40-d346-351a-b8b7-bb67c6089f2c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "305a7f78-f250-388d-aa23-8347aabfeac6", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.7"}, {"id": "32896c43-bf0f-3084-80bb-b05f659b4e9f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "79a7f8bdb159d9914b58740f3d31d602a6e4aca8 <d8cfe9f71d302970ae393616960f2b3021d2b3b0"}, {"id": "3c0b9bba-dc0e-3b29-87cf-8725822be243", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.57"}, {"id": "583290bc-7a9c-329a-b345-ea90a227b6c4", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "8938f2a1-5381-32ad-99e5-9bf8be2ba8cf", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "79a7f8bdb159d9914b58740f3d31d602a6e4aca8 <3408e98f06ce06ea6a58ca6c39da9c23f0029c06"}, {"id": "ac7bdc06-8482-3f4c-9f70-7fab34cf34da", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.160"}, {"id": "cc176b72-b630-3dda-a715-0deb47e478c5", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "79a7f8bdb159d9914b58740f3d31d602a6e4aca8 <9496d857205e60241034b798d7745ff8830ba599"}, {"id": "dc744a1f-08c4-354b-9716-393c4cd1fe6e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5.14"}, {"id": "e430a559-8a27-3f46-990d-b9a4dd369ffb", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "79a7f8bdb159d9914b58740f3d31d602a6e4aca8 <d05524794240b52fdc3b6c1220dd05505715824d"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "b604ef6d-e61f-3581-9dd8-3a0ae5c53fb8", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}